PPF is Concave Shaped
PPF is concave shaped because of increasing
marginal rate of transformation (MRT), i.e. more
and more units of one commodity'are sacrificed to
gain an additional unit of another commodity.MRT
increases because it is assumed that no resource is
equally efficient in production of all goods. As
resources are transferred from one good to another,
less and less efficient resources have to be
employed. This raises cost and raises MRT. In the
given example of guns and butter, units of guns
sacrificed keep on increasing each time to increase
production of one unit of butter.
